---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Copyright Information | Study Hub"
  description="Learn how original Study Hub content and third-party learning resources are treated, and how to raise a rights concern."
>
  <main class="legal-page">
    <header class="legal-page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Content and permissions</p>
      <h1>Copyright Information</h1>
      <p>Study Hub brings together original site content and learning materials from different authors and sources. Their rights remain with their respective owners.</p>
      <p class="policy-updated">Last updated <time datetime="2026-10-10">October 10, 2026</time></p>
    </header>

    <article class="legal-copy">
      <section>
        <h2>Original Study Hub content</h2>
        <p>The Study Hub name, site design, original descriptions, and original written material belong to their respective rights holders. Unless a page states otherwise, you may not republish or commercially reuse that original content without permission, except where applicable law allows.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Third-party learning resources</h2>
        <p>Study notes, examination papers, marking guides, images, and other files may be owned by their authors, schools, publishers, examination bodies, or other rights holders. Their presence in the library does not transfer ownership, certify their accuracy, or give you permission to redistribute them.</p>
        <p>Check the rights that apply before copying, adapting, or sharing a resource. Use materials for study in a manner consistent with the rights holder’s terms and applicable law.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Report a rights concern</h2>
        <p>If you believe a resource has been included without permission or is otherwise infringing your rights, email <a href="mailto:trusteth777@gmail.com?subject=Study%20Hub%20copyright%20concern">trusteth777@gmail.com</a>. Include the page or resource title, where it appears, your relationship to the rights, and enough detail for Study Hub to review the concern. Do not include sensitive information that is not needed to identify the material.</p>
        <p>Study Hub will review the information and may restrict or remove material while a concern is assessed. Please contact Study Hub if you need to provide additional information.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
